.* DSPSPLF: a spooled file's lines through a window the program moves
.* (F19/F20, the Control line), as text or in hexadecimal.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CTLCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FINDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 30'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=POSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 14'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LINECL BASETYPE='CHAR 78'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FLAGCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=FILE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=CTL CLASS=CTLCL.
:VAR NAME=FIND CLASS=FINDCL.
:VAR NAME=PAGELINE CLASS=POSCL.
:VAR NAME=COLS CLASS=POSCL.
:VAR NAME=RULER CLASS=LINECL.
:VAR NAME=LINE CLASS=LINECL.
:VAR NAME=FOLD CLASS=FLAGCL VALUE='N'.
:LISTDEF NAME=LINES VARS='LINE'.
:COND NAME=TRUNC EXPR='&FOLD. NE "Y"'.
:COND NAME=FOLDED EXPR='&FOLD. EQ "Y"'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/SPKEYS' NAME=SPKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F19 ACTION='RETURN 19'.F19=Left
:KEYI KEY=F20 ACTION='RETURN 20'.F20=Right
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=TRUNC.F11=Folded
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=FOLDED.F11=Truncated
:KEYI KEY=F14 ACTION='RETURN 14'.F14=Find options
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Find
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPSPLF KEYL=SPKEYS HELP=DSPSPLF ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=NONE BOTSEP=NONE.Display Spooled File
:DATA DEPTH=3.
:DATACOL WIDTH=16.
:DATACOL WIDTH=53.
:DATAC.File  . . . . . :   &FILE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/CTL' VAR=CTL USAGE=INPUT CSRLOC.Control
:DATAI HELP='FLD/FIND' VAR=FIND USAGE=INPUT.Find
:DATACOL WIDTH=26.
:DATAC.Page/Line   &PAGELINE.
:DATAC.Columns     &COLS.
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH=1.
:DATAC.&RULER.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LINES COMPACT.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LINE' VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPSPLF.Display Spooled File - Help
:P.The lines of a spooled file, page after page. Page up and down move
by a screen; F19 and F20 move the window left and right. On the
Control line, +n and -n move by lines, Pn goes to page n, Wn starts the
window at column n, T and B go to the top and the bottom, and *HEX
shows the bytes in hexadecimal (*CHAR goes back). F16 finds the text
typed on the Find line.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F19=Left
:PD.Left.
:PT.F20=Right
:PD.Right.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F11=Folded
:PD.Folded.
:PT.F11=Truncated
:PD.Truncated.
:PT.F14=Find options
:PD.Find options.
:PT.F16=Find
:PD.Find.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CTL'.Control
:P.Type the control.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FIND'.Find
:P.Type the find.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LINE'.LINE
:P.The line description.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
